  "body": "Part of #128.\n\nThe stdio MCP server (`crates/app/src/mcp/`) has gaps left over from #128's work (the hardening sat uncommitted in the stale `issue/128-mcp-server` worktree):\n\n- A JSON-RPC request with `\"id\": null` is treated as a request; JSON-RPC 2.0 says it is an invalid request.\n- `serve()` reads whole lines into a `String`: an unbounded line is held in memory in full, and a non-UTF-8 line ends the session with an I/O error instead of a parse error.\n- A misspelled field in a nested params patch (e.g. `clearance_z.ofset`) is silently ignored; only top-level typos are refused today.\n- The `post` tool reports the requested path rather than the path the post actually wrote.\n\nDone means: `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs` pins all four - a null id is an invalid request; a line over 16 MiB is a parse error, skipped without being held in memory, and the session reads on; a non-UTF-8 line is a parse error and the session reads on; a nested patch typo is refused naming its dotted path - and `post` returns the path written.\n",
